.TH MU2EDAQ\-TAG\-RELEASE 1 "2026-07-23" "Mu2e DAQ" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-tag\-release \- create, rename, or list release tags across mu2edaq\-main and all submodules
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh
.I tag
.RB [ \-m
.IR message ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-push ]
.br
.B mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh
.B \-\-rename
.I old\-tag new\-tag
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-push ]
.br
.B mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh
.B \-\-list
.RI [ pattern ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh
manages release tags across every submodule of the
.B mu2edaq\-main
meta-repository and the parent repository itself.
It supports three modes of operation: creating a new tag, renaming an existing
tag, and listing tags.
.PP
Tags are pushed to each repository's
.B origin
remote unless
.B \-\-no\-push
is specified.
If a repository already carries the requested tag it is skipped without error,
making create and rename operations safe to re-run after an interruption.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I tag
The tag name to create (e.g.\&
.BR p01.00.00 ).
Required in the default (create) mode.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m " message"
Annotation message for the tag.
Defaults to
.RI \(lq Release\ <tag> \(rq
when omitted.
Only relevant in create mode.
.TP
.B \-\-rename
Rename
.I old\-tag
to
.I new\-tag
across all repositories.
The new tag is created at the same commit as the old tag and preserves the
original annotation message.
The old tag is then deleted locally and on
.BR origin .
.TP
.B \-\-list
List tags in every repository.
Output can be filtered with an optional glob
.IR pattern .
Use
.B \-\-json
to format output as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Format
.B \-\-list
output as a JSON object keyed by repository name.
Each entry is an array of objects with fields
.BR tag ,
.BR commit
(7-character short hash),
.BR date ,
and
.BR message .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print every action that would be taken without creating, renaming, or pushing
any tags.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-push
Apply tag changes locally but do not push to
.BR origin .
The script prints the commands needed to push manually when this flag is used.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a tag and push immediately:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh p01.00.00
.EE
Create with a custom annotation message:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh p01.00.00 \-m "First production release"
.EE
Preview a tagging operation without making changes:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh p01.00.00 \-\-dry\-run
.EE
Create tags locally, inspect, then push manually:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh p01.00.00 \-\-no\-push
    git submodule foreach 'git push origin p01.00.00'
    git push origin p01.00.00
.EE
Rename a tag across all repositories:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh \-\-rename p01.00.00\-rc p01.00.00
.EE
Preview a rename without making changes:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh \-\-rename p01.00.00\-rc p01.00.00 \-\-dry\-run
.EE
List all tags in plain text:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh \-\-list
.EE
List tags matching a pattern:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh \-\-list 'p*'
.EE
List all tags as JSON:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh \-\-list \-\-json
.EE
List filtered tags as JSON, piped through a formatter:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-tag\-release.sh \-\-list 't*' \-\-json | python3 \-m json.tool
.EE
.SH BEHAVIOR
.SS Tag ordering
In create and rename modes, submodules are processed first in the order
returned by
.BR "git submodule foreach" .
The parent repository
.RB ( mu2edaq\-main )
is always last, so its tag points to a commit that already references
the tagged submodule states.
.SS Skipping existing tags
If the target tag already exists in a repository during a create or rename
operation, that repository is skipped and a
.B SKIP
message is printed.
This allows a failed run to be retried without manually cleaning up partial
results.
.SS Annotated tags
All tags created or copied by this script are annotated
.RB ( "git tag \-a" ),
recording tagger identity, date, and message in the git object database.
Lightweight tags are not created.
.SS JSON output
The
.B \-\-json
flag is only valid with
.BR \-\-list .
Output is a JSON object where each key is a repository name and each value is
an array of tag objects.
Repositories with no matching tags appear as empty arrays.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The requested operation completed successfully.
.TP
.B non-zero
A git operation failed.
The script exits immediately on the first error due to
.BR "set \-euo pipefail" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .gitmodules
Defines the submodule paths and remote URLs used by this script.
Located at the root of the
.B mu2edaq\-main
repository.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-bootstrap (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-update\-submodules (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR git\-tag (1),
.BR git\-submodule (1)
.SH REPOSITORY
.UR https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-main
https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-main
.UE
